  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a88974a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "After loading the raw Excel dataset, we immediately create an independent duplicate using the `.copy()` method. \n",
    "\n",
    "This is a critical best practice in data analytics. If we were to simply assign `df_clean = df`, both variables would point to the exact same object in the system memory. Any row deletions or filters applied to `df_clean` would permanently alter the original raw data as well. \n",
    "\n",
    "By using `.copy()`, we create a safe, isolated working environment (`df_clean`). The original dataset (`df`) remains completely untouched in the background as our \"Source of Truth.\" This prevents accidental data loss during the cleaning phase, avoids Pandas memory warnings, and saves computational resources, as we do not have to reload the large Excel file if we need to reference the raw data again."
   ]
  },
  {
