    "When looking at the initial descriptive statistics for the revenue column, two major anomalies stand out right away that require us to clean the data. \n",
    "\n",
    "First, the minimum and maximum values are exactly the same amount but with opposite signs (-168,469.60 and 168,469.60). In a real-world accounting or ERP system, this perfect symmetry usually means a massive billing error occurred and was immediately canceled out, or a huge order was fully returned. \n",
    "\n",
    "Second, because of these massive outliers on both ends, the standard deviation is extremely high at 428.12. This variance is completely disproportionate when you consider that the median transaction is only 11.80 and the mean is 20.86. The raw data is severely distorted by these rare events.\n",
    "\n",
    "By identifying and removing these canceled orders and extreme outliers, we get rid of the system noise. This is crucial for our project because our upcoming classification model needs to learn the structural tax patterns of actual, sustainable business transactions, not of rare data entry mistakes."
   ]
