    "\n",
    "Next, we applied a filter to keep only transactions where `Revenue`, `Quantity`, and `UnitPrice` are strictly greater than zero. This step reduced our dataset from 394,800 to 386,325 rows, meaning exactly 8,475 records were removed. \n",
    "\n",
    "We did this for a very practical business reason. While some of these dropped rows are the negative return transactions we noticed earlier, the vast majority are simply zero-revenue bookings. These could be free sample items, 100% discounts, or just incomplete entries in the system. \n",
    "\n",
    "Since our target variable is based on the post-tax profit margin, transactions with zero or negative revenue simply do not make sense for our analysis. You cannot calculate a meaningful profit margin from a free sample. By removing these 8,475 rows, we protect the integrity of our predictive model and ensure it only learns from actual, revenue-generating sales."
